{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c589","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae29-3706-76b3-a375-34fbf7476ffc"},"sequence":287,"recorded_at":1780531400000569,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"139fe689-449f-4637-a23d-49ec9bbe1fac","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"139fe689-449f-4637-a23d-49ec9bbe1fac","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"139fe689-449f-4637-a23d-49ec9bbe1fac"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2a-4a4b-7dd0-ab21-2c38a216ab99"},"task_id":"01a0ae2a-4a4b-7dd0-ab21-2c38a216ab99","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2a-4a4b-7dd0-ab21-2c38a216ab99","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-12-1\",\n  \"command\": \"/Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board worktree checkpoint --help 2>&1 | head -60\\necho \\\"====\\\"\\n/Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board spawn --help 2>&1 | head -60\",\n  \"description\": \"Check checkpoint and spawn syntax\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"Checkpoint an accepted Change Request revision.\\n\\nThe accepted candidate tree becomes one internal commit on the Story branch,\\ncreated under a compare-and-swap on the branch tip. The leaf remains integrating:\\nnothing is landed on trunk, and internal checkpoints only delimit later Task\\ndiffs and make the work recoverable before the final Story squash.\\n\\nA Change Request with repository_delta=empty creates no commit — its tree would\\nequal its parent's — and the leaf likewise remains integrating.\\n\\nOnly the tracked integration run bound to the accepted revision's producer role\\nand archetype may run this command. Reviewers, orchestrators, and other producer\\narchetypes are refused.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board worktree checkpoint <ELEMENT-ID> [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -h, --help   help for checkpoint\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \\\".task-board\\\")\\n      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite\\n      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)\\n      --json                     Output in JSON format\\n      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check\\n      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)\\n      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)\\n====\\nQueue an AI agent run (agy, claude, codex, gemini, muse, or qwen) for a board element.\\n\\nspawn.preferred_agentic_system is an optional provider allow-set. exclusive\\npins one provider; mixed retains runtime affinity when it belongs to the set or\\naccepts an explicit in-set --agent. Out-of-set providers are refused before\\ntask lookup or launch side effects. Legacy spawn.preferred_agent retains its\\nbest-effort preference behavior. Runtime affinity detects Codex from\\nCODEX_SESSION, CODEX_THREAD_ID, or CODEX_CI and otherwise selects Claude.\\nOptional spawn.schedule UTC windows temporarily replace the base provider set.\\nA provider or registered model outside the active window is refused before\\nside effects with the allowed set and a concrete retry step; the selected\\nprovider's ceiling is applied afterward.\\n\\nOn launch: assigns element to agent name, sets status from role config and\\nqueues a tracked background RUN. By default the public command returns\\nimmediately with observation commands. Pass --wait to block in the same process\\nuntil the RUN reaches a terminal state; no separate 'task-board spawn wait\\nRUN-...' invocation is needed. The --background flag is required so execution placement is explicit\\nat every callsite. A repeated spawn for an element that already has a queued or\\nrunning RUN returns that existing handle with Status: already_running and makes\\nno changes. Pass --allow-parallel to create another RUN intentionally.\\n\\nPrompt composition:\\n  Primary source of truth is the board:\\n    - Task description comes from the element README\\n    - Task-specific DoD comes from the element checklist\\n    - Instructions come from precondition resources attached to the element\\n\\n  Legacy compatibility overrides:\\n    --task-path FILE  Optional extra brief appended to the task description\\n    --dod-path FILE   Optional extra DoD lines appended to the prompt only\\n\\nThe prompt is always composed from the role template plus board state. Legacy\\nfile overrides only append extra context — they never replace role identity,\\nboard task context, FIRST/LAST status blocks, skills, or CLI reference.\\n\\nSafety:\\n  --instruction NAME  Validates that a precondition resource matching NAME\\n                      is linked to the task before spawning. Errors with a\\n                      helpful message if not found.\\n\\nPrompt file is auto-saved to .temp/prompts/ with timestamp naming.\\n\\nModel and reasoning selection:\\n  --model is required for every spawn of a role without a configured default.\\n  --reasoning-effort is required for Codex spawns.\\n  --reasoning-effort is required for Qwen spawns.\\n  --reasoning-effort is required for Claude spawns, except claude-haiku-4-5\\n  (and its dated snapshot), which take no effort at all.\\n  task-board never supplies model or reasoning defaults of its own. The only\\n  exception is a per-role default the project configured explicitly at\\n  spawn.ceilings.<provider>.roles.<role>.default_model and\\n  .default_reasoning_effort. That seed fills only the dimensions omitted at the\\n  callsite, an explicit flag always wins per dimension, and the seeded pair\\n  still passes the ordinary ceiling, so a default can never widen a bound. A\\n  role with no configured default keeps explicit selection mandatory. Inspect\\n  what a role resolves to before spawning with:\\n    task-board q 'project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER)'\\n  Inspect the current registry with: task-board q 'models(agent=codex)'\\n\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4851,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1213,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
